				"description": "# PayPal.me Payment Link Request\n\n## Overview\nThis request accesses a PayPal.me payment link, which provides a simplified way to request or send payments through PayPal. The endpoint returns an HTML page that facilitates PayPal transactions for the specified account (CMRFF).\n\n## Query Parameters\n\n### `country.x`\n- **Purpose**: Specifies the country context for the PayPal transaction\n- **Current Value**: `US` (United States)\n- **Usage**: Determines regional settings, currency options, and compliance requirements for the payment page\n\n### `locale.x`\n- **Purpose**: Sets the language and regional format for the PayPal interface\n- **Current Value**: `en_US` (English - United States)\n- **Usage**: Controls the display language and formatting conventions (date, currency symbols, etc.) on the payment page\n\n## Expected Response\n\n- **Status Code**: 200 OK\n- **Content Type**: HTML\n- **Response Body**: A fully-rendered HTML page containing:\n  - PayPal payment interface\n  - Account information for CMRFF\n  - Payment form and options\n  - PayPal branding and security elements\n  - Embedded scripts and stylesheets for functionality\n\n## Visualization\n\nThis request includes a **post-response visualization script** that creates an interactive dashboard displaying:\n\n- **Status Code**: HTTP response status\n- **Response Time**: Request duration in milliseconds\n- **Response Size**: Payload size in kilobytes\n- **Headers Count**: Number of response headers received\n\nThe visualization uses Chart.js to render a bar chart with PayPal's brand colors (#003087, #009cde, #00b4d8, #48cae4) for an enhanced visual representation of the response metrics."
